WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:15.000
to see their Majesties leave Buckingham Palace on the footed stakes.

00:15.000 --> 00:18.000
The cheer, its warmth is most evident.

00:18.000 --> 00:20.000
The Duke and Duchess of Gloucester.

00:20.000 --> 00:25.000
Then the Royal Coach draws up and from it outstep the King, the Queen and the Princesses.

00:25.000 --> 00:28.000
A high spot this for the crowd.

00:28.000 --> 00:30.000
The Royal farewells begin.

00:30.000 --> 00:33.000
To be plainly seen in all of them is sincerity.

00:33.000 --> 00:37.000
There's a catch at my throat as I see the Princesses curtsy to their grandeur.

00:37.000 --> 00:39.000
Even the train seemed impressionable.

00:39.000 --> 00:42.000
The Royal travellers go aboard.

00:42.000 --> 00:46.000
Their daughters go with them as far as Portsmouth.

00:46.000 --> 00:48.000
The arrival at Portsmouth.

00:48.000 --> 00:50.000
More meetings and partings.

00:50.000 --> 00:54.000
This is a big moment for the city. We're running very high.

00:54.000 --> 00:59.000
All possible points of vantage are strongly held by many more people than they can easily accommodate.

00:59.000 --> 01:02.000
And the King Admiral goes very good sub.

01:02.000 --> 01:05.000
The air is heavy with emotional loyalty.

01:05.000 --> 01:07.000
As sail.

01:07.000 --> 01:09.000
Aeroplanes dip in salute.

01:09.000 --> 01:11.000
A popular ballad.

01:11.000 --> 01:13.000
God send you back to me.

01:13.000 --> 01:25.000
And I don't think I'm the only one who thought of it either.

01:25.000 --> 01:27.000
These old Maytime customs are never ending.

01:27.000 --> 01:31.000
At Halston, down Cornwall Way, it's all different.

01:31.000 --> 01:33.000
The occasion affects everybody's feet.

01:33.000 --> 01:35.000
With an itch to dance and dance.

01:35.000 --> 01:36.000
And they do.

01:36.000 --> 01:38.000
All together in the floral dance idea.

01:38.000 --> 01:39.000
Can you see better now?

01:39.000 --> 01:44.000
So that the dancers may enter and leave luck and happiness behind by their visit.

01:44.000 --> 01:47.000
And the little dogs laugh fun when some couples run.

01:47.000 --> 01:51.000
At Halston, look as if it had put the clock back a hundred years.

01:51.000 --> 02:10.000
In fact, these old Mayday customs.

